        "title": "Dyeing and Fiber Arts - Landscape and Taxonomy",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Dyeing and fiber arts encompass the complete chain from raw animal or plant fiber to finished colored cloth: preparation, spinning, dyeing, and weaving. The technical core is **mordanting chemistry** — the coordination chemistry that makes color permanent. Without mordanting, most natural dyes wash out. With the right mordant, colors survive centuries."
    },
